    {
      "id": "claim_7c647e831652420887837c736358ad87",
      "statement": "Validation enforces six classes of rules: design element rules (IsDesign, row role), quantity/dimension rules (quantity type, dimensional components), product/specification rules (duplicate codes, spec rows), design-to-database alignment (DesignDB master, orphaned internals), position-specific rules (drivers, connectors), and template/structure rules (slots, exterior contexts).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/utils/validationRules.js#L177-L450",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b0a67cc2c1f42bfdac8fe12d9bc87f09552c10162ca3ab1b8ad06addc523d04:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_29d5e2cabbe64ad18cb3f2836cdb7a05",
      "statement": "Positions and position families can be marked as ignored via toggleIgnorePosition() or toggleIgnorePositionFamily(). Ignored positions drop out of validation scope immediately—their issues are filtered before results are returned. Delegated positions (those whose ExtRef names another position) are also treated as out-of-scope.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/ValidationFixModal.jsx#L62-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5a29cb52526737a6a79f503caad609898bd6fd0fa26768d414932ebac2280f7:"
