    {
      "id": "claim_ce1a37d1b38244e1a44bac1543b4a71a",
      "statement": "readiness() in readiness.js computes project completeness via four independent clauses: (1) every non-ignored position has a recipe, (2) every Form product is placed, (3) nothing blocks export (no blocking issues), (4) the three documents agree (DesignDB, Product Spec, Recipes). Each clause reports done, queued, remaining count, and detail. The project is done when all actionable clauses are done or queued.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/utils/readiness.js#L37-L147",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8e9f88d78103eec31ab6ae4abd9d81bdab6a44cd3437df3cd7879cd6db07dc1c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_330cce4ff28644c3adf834ee131be8a7",
      "statement": "A readiness clause is queued when the fix is staged in a change queue (e.g., DesignDB rows in queueMissingDbRows()) pending external action (Excel paste). Queued counts as done on the user's side. Once all clauses are done or queued, readiness.done is true.",
      "evidence": [
